        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lavinia Greenlaw, Nâzım Hikmet, Mehmed Ali Pasha, Ali Fuat Cebesoy, Oktay Rıfat Horozcu, Mehmet Ali Aybar, Andrew Cowan, Kathryn Hughes, Val Taylor\n- Organizations: UEA Creative Writing Course\n- Roles: poet, novelist, playwright, screenwriter, director, memoirist, statesman, activist, lawyer, athlete, course director\n\nFacts:\n- Nâzım Hikmet Ran was born on 15 January 1902 and died on 3 June 1963.\n- Nâzım Hikmet was commonly known as Nâzım Hikmet.\n- Nâzım Hikmet was a Turkish poet, playwright, novelist, screenwriter, director, and memoirist.\n- Lavinia Greenlaw was born on 30 July 1962.\n- Lavinia Greenlaw is an English poet and novelist.\n- Mehmed Ali Pasha was the grandfather of Ali Fuat Cebesoy.\n- Mehmed Ali Pasha was the great-grandfather of Nâzım Hikmet, Oktay Rıfat Horozcu, and Mehmet Ali Aybar.\n- Ali Fuat Cebesoy was a Turkish statesman.\n- Mehmet Ali Aybar was a socialist activist, lawyer, and athlete.\n- The UEA Creative Writing Course currently lists Andrew Cowan, Kathryn Hughes, Lavinia Greenlaw, and Val Taylor as course directors.",
